<title>INDIA: Indian soybean remain weak despite low arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean remain weak despite low arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained weak in thin central India on Thursday despite poor arrivals. Prices fell 100-150 rupees per tonne while arrivals totalled just 500 tonnes.</p>
<p>Traders said demand from processing plants was poor.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees per tonne today on increased offerings and soy oil refined remained steady in thin trading.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly up on increased export demand. Soymeal yellow was $305-306 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was $113-114 per tonne FAS west coast Indian ports for exports and was 3,900-3,925 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition.</p>
